## Deliverables

1. Redesigned **Startup** dashboard template (Rust template builder + any new painters/components)
2. UI that matches the fixed regions above
3. Graph controls: channel toggles, pause, zoom, auto-scroll
4. Status LEDs + empty-by-default warnings panel
5. Template version bump + default-dashboard refresh hook so existing installs pick it up
6. Brief CHANGELOG note under Unreleased

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Opening **Startup** always shows the same region map (status strip → primary → secondary → graph → LEDs → warnings)
- [ ] RPM / TPS / MAP / Lambda are the most prominent numbers
- [ ] Secondary grid slots remain reserved when channels are missing
- [ ] Strip chart updates smoothly live; pause freezes the series; zoom still works while paused
- [ ] Warnings panel is blank with no faults, populated only when there are active issues
- [ ] No designer / drag handles appear on this dash in normal use
- [ ] Updates do not freeze the UI under a typical full channel stream
- [ ] Works with Speeduino / rusEFI / epicEFI / FOME channel naming via aliases where already supported

---

## Visual Success Test

If you cover the labels, a tuner who uses the dash daily should still know **where** RPM, Lambda, CLT, and the graph live. The panel should feel like a race-engineer monitor: calm until something is wrong, then unmistakably loud only in the warnings / out-of-range values.

---

## Out of Scope for This Pass

- Editable layouts / user-saved rearrangements of this monitor
- Mixing this UI with VE table / 3D plot editing (Link’s full Tuning tab is not the goal)
- New ECU protocol features
- Mobile / phone layouts
